.TH "GIT-WORK" "1" "Apr 2019" "Generated from git-work's source code" ""

.SH NAME
git-work-schema-log - Print the schema's history


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-work schema log [KEY] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the schema's history: every operation of every type and field entity,
one JSON object per line, oldest first within each entity. With a KEY, only
that entity's.

.PP
This is what says who added a status and when. KEY is a type key or a field
key, /\&.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-f\fP, \fB--format\fP="json"
	Select the output formatting style. Valid values are [json,text]

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for log


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
git work schema log
git work schema log task/status
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-work-schema(1)\fP
